<title>UK: Jasmin wins contracts worth 4.5 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Jasmin wins contracts worth 4.5 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jasmin Plc said on Tuesday it had won several contracts from regular customers worth a total of around 4.5 million stg.</p>
<p>The orders include a contract from the British Ministry of Defence and a 25 percent increase in value on the five million stg order for passenger information and communication for the new Northern Line London Underground trains from GEC Alsthom Metro-Cammell Ltd.</p>
<p>They also included an order for detection equipment from the Far East.</p>
<p>The company also announced that it will be appointing a new non-executive director in the near future, Tony Caplin, who is currently Chairman of Browns Plc.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
